Conclusion: the top chunk's size field (at buffer+BUFSIZE) is attacker bytes
on attack/readback (0x584543432d454853, 0x41414141b3010000) and intact on
safe (0x205e1). Yet main_arena.top stays 0x555556620a20 at every malloc entry
and at the terminal free, and every returned pointer is at most
0x55555640ce10 — 80800 bytes (0x13ba0) *before* data->buffer 0x5555564209b0,
never in the overflow region [buffer+BUFSIZE, buffer+BUFSIZE+3976]. The
post-parse allocations come from earlier free chunks, not from the corrupted
top; no allocatable object is carved out of attacker-controlled overflow
bytes. Rung 3 and rung 4 unchanged; no pointer or rung-5 claim.

`gdb-late-malloc.cmd` was additionally run unchanged on attack.gxf and
readback.gxf at 09:39Z: it logged the same 5 and 12 malloc sizes with top
still P at every entry. Raw captures were kept in the gitignored site, not
in the committed lab tree.
